# The backend image builds from the repo root (it needs the root Directory.Build.props and global.json).
# Allow-list only what it needs.
*
!Directory.Build.props
!global.json
# The analyzer settings, including the exemption for EF's generated migrations. Without it the publish
# inside the image is held to different rules than the build outside it, and fails on generated code.
!.editorconfig
# ST-063: the note prompt is embedded in the API assembly, so it is an input to this build. Only the
# prompt itself; the fixtures, the eval harness and the virtualenv beside it are not.
!research/
research/*
!research/prompts/
research/prompts/*
!research/prompts/note_v2.md
# ST-061: and the character data DraftValidator reads text with, which is embedded beside it.
!research/prompts/unicode-tables.json
# ST-063: and the note schema, which the Claude provider sends as its structured-output format.
!research/prompts/schema.json

!backend/
backend/**/bin/
backend/**/obj/
backend/tests/

# Local settings and secrets. They are git-ignored, so a clean clone has none, but a developer's
# working copy can, and `COPY backend/src/` would carry them into the image, where the API would load
# them. No appsettings file is committed and the image needs none: every setting reaches the container
# from its environment (deploy/api.env.example). If one is ever committed for the image, allow it here
# by name, after these lines.
backend/**/appsettings*.json
backend/**/launchSettings.json
backend/**/*.binlog
**/secrets.json
**/*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
